  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing CRM Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the user\'s needs for a solar installation CRM. I\'m prioritizing the schema they provided and mapping out the core functionalities: form creation, data input, and project management. Initial thoughts focus on how to structure the system to best capture solar-specific details.\n\n\n**Defining Core System Sections**\n\nI\'ve moved on to defining the essential sections within the CRM. Specifically, I\'m focusing on \"Customers\" and \"Projects,\" ensuring that the data structure accommodates essential details like contact information, Aadhar, branch (configurable!), and location. For \"Projects,\" I\'m incorporating fields such as capacity, type, vendor, and various technical identifiers, considering how to make the fields customizable or toggleable to meet the varied needs of installers. Project stages are also being considered, and how to allow for 3 to 15 stages.\n\n\n**Detailing Project Financials**\n\nI\'m now detailing the project financials within the CRM, including fields for quoted amounts, received payments, and automatic calculation of receivables, alongside discounts and payment types. The system will allow users to skip this section if it is not relevant to a given project. I\'m also adding fields for Subsidy Status History, with status (rejected/approved/pending), date, and reason, and Bank Info.\n\n\n**Implementing Quick Actions**\n\nI\'m now integrating quick actions directly into the customer view, displaying their name and phone number for immediate dialing. I\'m also adding \"Add\" buttons within each section, enabling users to swiftly add records, like payments or project details. I am also working on dynamic field toggling, allowing users to customize their view by hiding or displaying fields they don\'t use, like POC or specific branch details.\n\n\n**Integrating Firebase**\n\nMy focus is now on integrating Firebase for robust data storage, given the need for durable cloud persistence of customer and project data. I\'m exploring Firestore for storing customer details, project data, financial records, and subsidy history. I\'m also considering Firebase Authentication if required. I need to review `/skills/system_skills/firebase-skill/SKILL.md` to ensure I have the information I need, specifically, the Firestore schema and auth management information.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Offline Capabilities**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a robust offline-first/localStorage client-side application. I am considering a highly interactive and polished CRM that saves data locally. I\'m exploring an approach that includes full export/import capabilities and beautiful state management. I\'ve confirmed that Firebase isn\'t installed or configured, which supports local storage for now. I\'m considering if this is a simple prototype or a full cloud app, the answer will determine next steps.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 729671709
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
