    thinking: "**Initiating Design Phase**\n\nI\'m starting the application design process now. I\'ve begun by examining the `metadata.json` file. Specifically, I\'ve noted that the `name` field is currently empty. This is consistent with the initialization checklist, which indicates that I need to update this field.\n\n\n**Defining CRM Structure**\n\nI\'m now focusing on structuring the \"Solar Project CRM\". I\'ve updated `metadata.json` with the name and a description. I\'m planning a modular approach, with type definitions in `src/types.ts`, initial data/configurations in `src/initialData.ts`, and component subdirectories in `src/components/` for maintainability. The core CRM feature set will include dynamic field settings to allow users to customize their view, as per the user\'s specific request to edit and remove any fields they do not need.\n\n\n**Implementing Field Control**\n\nI\'m now implementing the dynamic field settings feature. A \"Form Config / Field Settings\" panel will appear to the user. This lets the user control field visibility, immediately hiding fields across the application when toggled off. This is very powerful for customizing the CRM as requested.\n\n\n\n**Designing Project Progress**\n\nI\'m now integrating a project stage tracker with a visual progress bar for each project, for easy status review. I\'m also focusing on the data modules with \"Add/Edit\" buttons for each section. I\'ve designed the user requests for customizable customer details and project details including an automatically generated Project ID. Finally, I\'m working on the design for editable project stages, allowing from 3 to 15 stages with customizable definitions.\n\n\n**Adding Financial Calculations**\n\nI\'m now integrating financial modules with auto-calculations. The system tracks `quoted_amt`, `received`, `discount`, and `receivable`. I\'ve added a list of Payments with fields like Date, Amount, Payment Type, and Status, dynamically updating financial calculations. I\'m also adding Subsidy Status History with fields for tracking subsidy approvals (status, date, reasons). I\'ve added bank account information to the CRM. The \"approve/delete\" UI action, as requested by the user, is next.\n\n\n**Implementing UI/UX Refinement**\n\nI\'m implementing approval/verification and deletion actions across records with badge displays and confirmation dialogs. A gorgeous dashboard layout is underway, featuring a sidebar/filter area, a central panel, and a \"Quick Contact\" section at the top. I\'ve confirmed correct Tailwind CSS configuration with index.css and am starting with type definitions in `src/types.ts` for a fully type-safe CRM structure. I\'m also ensuring all icons are sourced from `lucide-react`. The dependencies are confirmed as React 19, Motion, Lucide icons, Tailwind, and Vite.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 13
      nanos: 178375766
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
