  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the React App**\n\nI\'ve got the API and Vite integration up and running smoothly, which is great! Now, I\'m focusing on designing the React app, specifically `/src/App.tsx`. The user wants a visually stunning design, so I\'m thinking about clean lines, and an immediately attention-grabbing look. I\'m starting with core functionality, with a user-focused experience.\n\n\n**Outlining CRM Customization**\n\nI\'m now outlining section-by-section requirements. Top section is for client contact info, and is followed by clear section description. The next is the interactive customization form. Module 1, the Customers Module, has various fields. I am including inline toggles, switches, and actions to customize its contents. I\'ve also incorporated an option to add custom fields based on client input. I\'m moving on to Module 2 for Projects Module customization.\n\n\n**Defining Project Pipeline Stages**\n\nI\'m deep in Module 3 now, mapping out the project pipeline stages customization. I\'m focusing on the interactive pipeline designer, allowing clients to define their stages and manage their order, with clear validation. I\'ve built in stage name editing, reordering, and deletion, and added a dynamic constraint for 3 to 15 stages. I\'m also including a toggle to optionally incorporate financial approval milestones. I\'m moving on to Module 4, for financial customization.\n\n\n**Visualizing Financial Flow**\n\nI\'m now visualizing the financial flow. I plan to use an elegant diagram showing how \"Quoted - Discount - Paid = Receivable\" is automatically calculated. It\'s important the client understands and approves this feature! I\'ve added a \"Payment Type\" field toggle and customizable \"Payment Methods\" with an \"Add Payment Mode\" option. Module 5, Subsidy Status History, has been defined with \"rejected/approved/pending, date, reason\" fields and a module-wide toggle. Module 6 focuses on Bank & Loan info and includes similar toggles and custom fields. Finally, I\'ve got a live schema blueprint preview on a right sidebar to display these features visually.\n\n\n**Visualizing Real-Time Schema Updates**\n\nI\'ve been working on a real-time visual database structure that updates dynamically as the user customizes the CRM. I\'m focusing on crafting a very informative and user-satisfying experience. I\'ve structured tables for `customers`, `projects`, `project_stages`, `financials`, `subsidy_history`, and `bank_info`. Each table clearly lists columns, data types, and \"Included\" or \"Custom\" badges, allowing the client to fully understand the architecture they are building! I\'m adding a \"Generate Custom CRM Architecture Proposal\" button, which will trigger an API call.\n\n\n**Implementing Submit Requirements**\n\nI\'m now implementing the submit requirements feature with a success message for local saving. I\'ve also incorporated a visually appealing slate-themed dashboard with a scrolling configuration layout and modern Tailwind typography. I\'m focusing on high-quality component code for a professional feel. I\'m designing default fields and stages, pre-filled with professional defaults. The default Customer Fields are: Name (required), Phone (required), Email (optional), Aadhar (optional with toggle), and POC (optional with toggle).\n\n\n**Defining Default Fields**\n\nI\'m now defining the default CRM fields. For customer information, I\'m including Branch, Location, and Address, all optional. Project fields cover Capacity, Type, Vendor, Meter Category, EB Number, and optional DTR Code, Sanctioned Load, DISCOM Division, Google Docs Link, and Location Link. I\'ve also set up the default Project Stages: Lead Discussion, Engineering Design, Net Metering, Material Procurement, Installation, Inspection, and Subsidy Claim. I\'m moving onto Financial, Subsidy, and Bank Info fields.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now write the full implementation for `/src/App.tsx`. It features:\n1. **Client Contact Module**: Quick input at the top to capture client name, email, phone, and company.\n2. **Interactive CRM Blueprint Customization**: Line-by-line switches for every schema field with helpful notes (e.g., branch, point of contact, discom div).\n3. **Point of Contact (POC) & Branch Logic**: Direct implementation of the user\'s specific rules (e.g., \"do you have more than 1 branch\", \"poc use for your pipeline\").\n4. **Interactive Pipeline Stage Designer**: Allows adding, re-ordering, renaming, and deleting project stages (3 to 15 stages check) and toggling the financial stage milestone.\n5. **Auto-calculating Financial Visualizer**: Demonstrates the automated payments calculation (Quoted - Discount - Received = Receivable) in a clean flow.\n6. **Live Schema Blueprint Preview**: A real-time updating schema model showing database tables, constraints, column types, and custom additions.\n7. **AI Proposal Generator**: Uses the server-side Gemini endpoint (`gemini-3.5-flash`) to generate a complete technical CRM blueprint and printable implementation proposal, with copy and print capabilities."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 11
      nanos: 355667132
    }
  }
}
