  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Form**\n\nI\'m working on the initial form design for the Solar CRM clients. My focus is on creating a highly polished, interactive experience. I\'ve begun to translate the client\'s requirements, specifically noting that the form should not gather specific details. This shift will require a rethink of the data intake process, while ensuring the end result is still effective.\n\n\n**Refining the Client Form**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a client-facing form, not a full CRM. My goal is to create a polished React app using Tailwind CSS and Lucide icons. I\'ll make sure it\'s password-protected, with the client initially setting the access code and a sun logo. This is more of an intake form. The design will use simple HTML, CSS, and JS. I\'ll need to remove the \"admin\" interface elements. I want to build a simple, effective, and elegant form.\n\n\n**Implementing Password Protection**\n\nI\'ve decided to implement a hardcoded password, `solar123`, for initial access. I\'ll include a beautifully styled startup prompt if the user is not logged in. I\'m now reading `src/App.tsx` to build the interactive client requirements configuration form, focusing on visual quality. I\'ll follow the provided guidelines for a clean, high-contrast light theme, utilizing Lucide\'s `Sun` or `SunDim` icon for the logo and line-by-line configuration form.\n\n\n**Defining Form Fields**\n\nI\'m now diving into defining the form\'s specific fields, especially the customer and project sections. I\'m focusing on interactive toggles and options to tailor the form based on client-specific needs. The goal is to build a project stages section that clients can fully configure, and I\'ll include buttons for custom fields and status toggles for standard ones.\n\n\n**Defining More Form Fields**\n\nI\'m now detailing the form sections: Stages (project), Financials, Subsidy Status History, and Bank Info. I\'m focusing on \"skip if not needed\" options for flexibility, automatic financial calculations, and clear status toggles. I\'m including checkboxes and selectors for payment methods and subsidy status, and the automatic project ID generation is noted. The final goal is to create a blueprint summary upon submission.\n\n\n"
