  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining The Approach**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got it. I\'m now realizing that Vite\'s built-in dev server, combined with the custom API server plugin injected into its config, eliminates the need for a separate Express server. This streamlines the setup considerably; no need for a separate server process. The plugin in `vite.config.ts` handles the API now.\n\n\n**Implementing The Backend**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing a robust backend. The current thinking is to create a custom `server.ts` Express backend, as suggested by the \"Full-Stack Applications (Express + Vite)\" instructions, to ensure the API endpoint `/api/generate-proposal` is securely hosted in production. I\'ll modify the `package.json` scripts to include \"dev\", \"build\", and \"start\" options using `tsx`, `vite build`, `esbuild`, and `node`, respectively. I need to make this production-ready.\n\n\n**Securing The Application**\n\nI\'m now implementing password protection. The goal is to create a secure gate screen with a hardcoded password, `solar123`, for initial access. The user wants it password protected, so I\'m aiming for a polished gate. My plan is to store the new password persistently in `localStorage` after they make a new password for it. There is also a settings panel for admin only users to change the password.\n\n\n**Designing The Interface**\n\nI\'m now designing the user interface. It will feature a header with an animated sun icon and client details. The main layout will have an interactive specification checklist on the left and a live schema builder preview on the right. This includes sections like client identity. The checklist will dynamically update the preview as users adjust inputs.\n\n\n**Configuring The Tables**\n\nI\'m now diving into the table configurations, specifically the Customers and Projects tables. For Customers, I\'m setting up toggles and dropdowns to dynamically modify the schema based on user choices. I\'m focusing on \"branch\" removal if multiple branches are not tracked. For POC, I\'m setting options to keep, repurpose, or delete the field. I\'m using checkboxes for field selection and adding \"Approve Section\" and \"Add Custom Field\" buttons. I\'m configuring similar controls for the Projects table.\n\n\n**Structuring The Project Phases**\n\nI\'m now detailing the project phases. My focus is structuring the phases for the proposal. The user can add, reorder, remove, and rename phases from 3 to 15, and they can also choose whether to include a financial verification stage. There are checkboxes too. I will be incorporating all of these details into the design.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 110133148
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
