  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Assessing Project Structure**\n\nI find the project structure exceptionally neat and well-defined. I\'m now carefully reviewing the user\'s feedback, especially their request to use simple HTML, CSS, and JS, along with a library like Lucide.\n\n\n**Refining Tool Focus**\n\nI now understand this isn\'t a CRM builder, but a crucial discovery questionnaire. The form itself is the core deliverable! My focus shifts to making it a clean, line-by-line experience with prominent \"Approve\" and \"Delete\" toggles for each field. I\'m exploring how to elevate the visual presentation of these elements.\n\n\n**Clarifying Field Functionality**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"Add Anyone\" feature. This expands the form\'s flexibility significantly. Adding a client\'s name and phone number on top is intuitive for easy contact. Each section gets an \"Add Custom Field / Add Anyone\" button, promoting user customization, which is exactly how this should go!\n\n\n**Implementing Password Protection**\n\nI\'m now integrating password protection. The \"admin side\" is completely out. The application will be a single page. On load, a password prompt appears. Once the password is correct, the form is visible! I\'m adding a sun logo in the top-left corner, as requested.\n\n\n**Enhancing User Experience**\n\nI\'m now thinking about how to make password management elegant. I\'ve decided on \"solar123\" as a hardcoded default password, but also a setting gear icon for changing the password and saving it to `localStorage`. I\'m focused on a secure and visually appealing password input. Furthermore, after form submission, instead of an admin list, a polished \"Configuration Summary\" is displayed. It will be able to copy the output, download it as a PDF/JSON, and generate a technical proposal via Gemini AI! This \"Generate Technical Proposal\" feature will call the server-side Gemini API we set up in `/api/generate-proposal`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 258536396
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
