    thinking: "**Analyzing Password Protection**\n\nI\'m currently focused on implementing password protection within `src/App.tsx`. The core requirement is hardcoding a password; once set, this password will be the only one accepted for access. This is a straightforward requirement, so I am beginning work on it.\n\n\n**Implementing Access Control**\n\nI\'ve decided to implement a clean password lock screen on startup if the user isn\'t authenticated. The default password will be \"solar123\", but can be set by the user later. I\'m storing the password in `localStorage` under the key `solar_crm_access_password`. I\'ve started the implementation with the initial state and local storage retrieval for the password.\n\n\n**Refining Authentication Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating robust authentication, managing correct password entry to grant application access, and storing authentication status via `sessionStorage`. Successful authentication calls `setIsAuthenticated` and grants access. I\'m also adding a password change input for the user, and ensuring the new password is saved to local storage for persistence.\n\n**Updating Visual Branding**\n\nI\'m changing the header logo to a spinning, glowing gold `Sun` icon from Lucide, replacing the sparkles for a more cohesive look. I will ensure proper import and integration of the `Sun` and `SunDim` icons.\n\n\n**Eliminating Admin View**\n\nI\'m removing the \"Admin\" tab entirely to meet the user\'s requirement. Instead of an admin interface, I\'m now integrating an inline \"Result/Success Spec View\" directly after form submission, offering a more streamlined and secure user experience. This view will display confirmation, the CRM database schema, pipeline stages, payment modes, and a unique AI Proposal button, calling the `/api/generate-proposal` endpoint.\n\n\n**Refactoring the Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a complete overhaul of the display. The goal is elegant presentation of the document directly on the page, incorporating copy-to-clipboard and print options for immediate client utility. I plan to use a single-view, single-page approach, which aligns perfectly with the app\'s streamlined focus. I need to inspect the current form structure, so I will determine if I should edit `/src/App.tsx` directly, or completely rewrite it.\n\n\n**Reviewing File Structure**\n\nI\'m now carefully examining the `src/App.tsx` file for context on imports and structure, before implementing the document display overhaul. I am paying close attention to the existing imports, especially for `lucide-react` icons. I\'m adding `Sun` and `LockKeyhole` icons. I am also making sure I understand the current approach to generating proposals from the client side, and will set up the fetch call to the `/api/generate-proposal` endpoint.\n\n\n**Constructing Proposal Payload**\n\nI\'m now building the payload for the `/api/generate-proposal` endpoint. I\'m focusing on the `handleGenerateProposal` function, extracting the necessary client data and section details from the `ClientSubmission` object. I\'m preparing the data for the `customers` and `projects` sections, including handling optional fields like `poc` and `branch`. I\'m using `useState` hooks for error management and display. I am also working on `setIsGeneratingProposal`, `setProposalError`, and `setProposalResult`.\n\n\n**Mapping Section Data**\n\nI\'m now mapping the incoming data, focusing on creating the payloads for `/api/generate-proposal`. I\'m extracting and structuring data for the `projects`, `stages`, `financials`, and `subsidy` sections. My current work involves ensuring the inclusion of active fields and payment methods from the submission data. I am using `.map` and `.filter` appropriately to transform and structure this data efficiently.\n\n\n**Designing Lock Screen**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the visual design for the lock screen. I\'m aiming for a soft, warm off-white background to give it a welcoming feel. The screen will be the first thing a user sees, so a clean and user-friendly interface is a priority. I need to make sure the input field for the password is clean and modern, and the display on startup is elegant.\n\n\n**Designing Portal Lock Screen**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the lock screen\'s design and functionality. The goal is a welcoming, secure entry point featuring a central, glowing sun logo and a clean password input field with a lock icon. I\'m incorporating a clear default passcode hint for ease of use, followed by the main portal display, which includes a glowing \"Sun\" logo on the top left. The top right displays \"Client Spec Profile\" with client name and phone. I\'m focusing on rewriting `/src/App.tsx` completely to achieve a pristine, single-view layout that integrates the password gate and proposal generation seamlessly. I\'m making sure it\'s as fast, clean and simple as possible.\n\n\n"
