tructure. Each section will have **Add** and **Delete** buttons for customization. There\'s an \"Add Custom Field\" button at the bottom of each section for client-defined fields with custom names and types. Project Stages and Financial Tags will both provide dynamic input with \"Add\" and \"Delete\" actions. I will ensure they also have a \"I don\'t know / Skip\" option to bypass. Finally, I will review `App.tsx`.\n\n\n**Crafting Perfect Interface**\n\nI am now focused on creating a beautiful user interface. I\'m prioritizing a clean, modular `App.tsx` file to replace the existing complex code. I\'ve designed a clear React app structure, including a header with a sun icon and a tagline. The main layout will be a single-view, responsive form with elegant typography and high contrast, clean spacing. I plan to incorporate a subtle lock button for secure developer admin access.\n\n\n**Building Interactive Fields**\n\nI\'m now implementing the interactive builder controls for each form field, with approve/delete actions and styling. Approved fields will feature an active border and checkmark, while deleted ones will have a strikethrough. I\'m also adding \"Field Notes\" for special requests and quick branch queries to streamline customer setup. I\'m focused on the workflow, using sidebar step indicators for each of the five core form sections.\n\n\n**Defining Field Logic**\n\nI am now implementing the field-level logic, starting with a crucial \"POC\" (Point of Contact) field, which will dynamically display a message prompting deletion if not applicable. I\'ve integrated a beautifully animated inline form accessed through the \"+ Add Custom Field\" button within sections. Under \"Projects,\" clean rows of technical fields are now presented with a delete functionality to tailor to the client\'s needs, complemented by the custom field addition feature. The \"Project Stages\" section is meticulously designed with dynamic panels for custom steps, and an \"I don\'t know / Sk