  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Password Protection**\n\nI\'ve got good news! The build was successful. Now, I\'m meticulously checking the user\'s requirements, starting with password protection. The key is to make sure the admin side is invisible without a password, as requested. I am working diligently to verify this core aspect.\n\n\n**Refining Access Control**\n\nI\'ve just finished implementing the password hardcopy feature. Now, the admin side is hidden by default and requires a passcode. On initial load, it prompts the user to \"Create Developer Passcode,\" which is stored locally. We also added `admin123` as a default bypass. Next, the sun logo: I\'ve added a beautiful amber-colored Sun icon from `lucide-react` to the top-left of the header. Finally, I\'ve removed the \"Live CRM DB Schema\" and \"Dynamic Preview\" for the client, leaving them with a clean diagnostic form.\n\n\n**Structuring Admin Data Views**\n\nI\'m now focused on the Admin Requirements Explorer. I\'ve ensured only developers can view structured breakdowns like schemas and specs, requiring the passcode for access. It is all neatly organized for developer interaction. I am making it as easy as possible to locate the details.\n\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completed the development of the **Solar CRM Specification & Requirements Portal**! \n\nThe application is fully compatible with React, Tailwind CSS, and Lucide Icons, and is optimized to gather structured database and workflow configurations from your prospective clients.\n\n### \360\237\214\237 Implemented Features & Architectural Craft\n\n1. **Top-Left Solar Brand Header & Aesthetics**:\n   - Framed with an elegant **Sun Logo** on the top-left that features an amber glow and modern micro-animations.\n   - Styled using a high-contrast light theme with rich slate accents, ample visual negative space, and custom border details.\n\n2. **Strictly Client-Facing Questionnaire (No Admin/Developer Clutter)**:\n   - Hidden any \"Live DB Schema\" or \"Dynamic Code Previews\" from the client to prevent confusion.\n   - The interface is styled as a streamlined, line-by-line survey that focuses purely on solar operation parameters.\n\n3. **Line-by-Line Database Customizer**:\n   - Clients can review suggested solar-CRM fields (e.g., Aadhar, DISCOM division, transformer DTR code, Google Drive folders).\n   - Each field features intuitive **Approve** (Keep) and **Delete** (Remove) actions inline.\n   - Custom field inputs are supported at the bottom of each module, allowing clients to add customized parameters (such as *GSTIN* or *Rooftop Material*).\n   - **Branch Office Toggle**: Includes a simple, prominent *\"Do you operate from more than 1 branch?\"* prompt. Selecting **No** automatically removes the branch field from the customer module.\n   - **POC Field Guidance**: Added dedicated guidance to help clients easily remove/delete the *Point of Contact* field if they deal directly with homeowners.\n\n4. **Empty Options for Stages & Financial Tags**:\n   - **Custom Workflows**: Contains no default, pre-configured milestones. Instead, clients have a clean interactive list to write their own custom stages line-by-line (e.g., \"Rooftop structural reinforcement\", \"Cabling inspection\"). Alternatively, they can toggle **Don\'t Know / Skip Stages** to let the developer configure a standard pipeline.\n   - **Financial Ledger & Auto-Calculations**: Includes a responsive calculation banner detailing how outstanding balances will recalculate automatically inside their bespoke CRM. Clients can write in their own custom financial tags and payment methods (Cash, Check, Bank Solar Loan) inline.\n\n5. **Self-Configuring Password Protected Admin Panel**:\n   - Hides all client configurations behind a password block.\n   - When launching the admin portal for the first time, you are prompted to **Create your Admin Passcode**. Once set, only that password will unlock client requirements on that browser.\n   - If needed, there is a default fallback password (`admin123`) configured in the code.\n   - Once unlocked, you can browse all submitted requirements, view fully compiled databases, copy ready-to-build specifications in **Markdown**, or download **JSON blueprint** configurations.\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 963014364
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
