ncialStageName` state to drive its value, while also ensuring the placeholder text functions correctly. I am now working on ensuring proper styling to maintain visual consistency. I am ensuring that the styling fits with the existing design system.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Preview**\n\nI\'ve implemented the financial stage preview section. I\'ve integrated a visual display using a circle with a dollar sign and the stage name, or a default text if none is entered. The styling seems to be working, I\'ve used Tailwind classes for consistent design and ensured dynamic updates with the `financialStageName` state. I\'m satisfied the display works well with either the custom stage name or the default fallback.\n\n\n**Designing the UI**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the design for the banking details section to improve its clarity and user experience. I\'m focusing on crafting a concise toggle layout using existing styling, similar to the existing button design for the financial stage. I intend to use \"Banking Enabled\" and \"Skipped / Omitted\" as the button text for simplicity. I\'m working on ensuring the style matches the design system.\n\n\n**Crafting the Buttons**\n\nI\'ve decided on the button text: \"Yes, Keep Banking & Loan Details\" and \"No, Skip Banking & Loan Details,\" aiming for clarity. I\'ve implemented the conditional styling, leveraging the existing design system for visual consistency. Now I\'m focused on the button layout using Tailwind.\n\n\n**Implementing the Toggle**\n\nI\'m now creating the banking details toggle buttons, using the code snippet for styling guidance. I\'m focusing on ensuring proper integration within the existing layout. My plan is to add the new UI elements for the banking option beneath the financial stage section, maintaining a consistent flow and using states from `App.tsx` from lines 50-90.\n\n\n**Updating the Declarations**\n\nI\'ve updated the `stagesStatus` initialization and state declaration to match the new type definition. I\'ve also incorporated branch management states and the `financialStageName` state within the state declaration section.\n\nI\'m now considering the best placement for the branch-related handlers, `handleAddBranch` and `handleRemoveBranch`, aiming for logical organization within the component. I\'ll test them next.\n\n\n**Appending Branch Details**\n\nI\'ve made a key discovery! I realized I can append branch names to the markdown output if multiple branches are specified, specifically within the customer section. I\'ve updated the `getRawMarkdown` function in `App.tsx` (lines 397-463) to include this new feature. I\'m adding `Operating Branches: [branch list]` to the customer section based on the branch list.\n\n\n"
