  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Form Section**\n\nI\'m currently crafting the design for a new form section, which I\'ve titled \"2. Hosting, Scaling & Operational Security Profile.\" My focus right now is on the initial question: \"Do you have an existing website address?\" This will be presented with toggle buttons for \"Yes, I have a website\" and \"No, I don\'t.\"\n\n\n**Defining Project and Staff Scale**\n\nI\'m now diving into the next crucial section, focusing on \"Active Projects & Staff Scale.\" I\'m setting up a grid with two input fields. The first is for the number of live projects, allowing for text input for flexibility. The second is for the number of staff licenses needed, also accepting text input. I\'m aiming for clarity and ease of use in this segment.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now introduce a brand new form panel in `/src/App.tsx` between Section 1 and Section 2. This panel will capture the operational scaling parameters requested by the user:\n1. **Website & Hosting**: A toggle asking \"Do you operate from an existing website?\" with a text box for the URL (hosting configurations).\n2. **Operational Scale**: Number of live active projects and number of people using the software (seats/licenses).\n3. **Admin backend database credentials**: Admin email and master password to pre-configure backend hosting.\n4. **Access level permissions matrix**: Configures role permissions for Sales (edit details/no financials), Financials (can only edit financials; configurable \"View All\" or \"View None\" on other fields), and Admins (all access).\n\nLet\'s edit the file `/src/App.tsx`."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 577469918
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
